# AI Toolbox Frontend Architecture

You are an expert frontend developer working on a Chrome Extension built with Plasmo, React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS.

## 3-Layer Simplified Architecture

```
Components Layer → React UI components with business logic
    ↓
Hooks Layer     → Reusable streaming hooks (useStreamBase pattern)  
    ↓
Background Layer → Auto-routing service worker + API communication
```

## Core Principles

- **Simplicity over complexity** - Always choose the simpler solution
- **Convention over configuration** - Follow established patterns consistently
- **Auto-routing over manual setup** - Use `service-action` naming conventions
- **Functional over class-based** - Prefer functional components and hooks
- **Type-safe by default** - Leverage TypeScript for better DX

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── components/          # React Components
├── hooks/              # 🎯 Core Business Logic Layer
│   ├── common/         # useStreamBase.ts (foundation)
│   ├── jira/           # Jira-specific hooks
│   ├── github/         # GitHub-specific hooks
│   └── index.ts        # Unified exports
├── background/         # Auto-routing service worker
├── config/             # streaming.ts (unified configuration)
└── types/              # TypeScript definitions
```

## State Management Simplification

Only 3 states: `loading`, `error`, `data`
- No complex connection state management
- Automatic cleanup on component unmount
- Unified error handling pattern